{{!--
  resume.md.hbs — renders one prepared resume (mvp-spec §3 F7). Every
  statement carries the claim label(s) it cites (C1, C2, … — each claim's
  place in career-profile.json's claims[]), so the validator and the person
  can check each line against the career profile. The runner's exporter
  renders this template, then strips the citation markers: the Markdown,
  DOCX and PDF a person sends carry none, and diff-v<n>.md keeps every
  statement's citations and source claims (mvp-spec F7: citations are
  stripped only at export).

  Nothing from the job posting renders here: a posting is data, never
  document text (hard-problems.md #3), so there is no "prepared for" line.

  Render context (runner/export/document.ts, ResumeModel):
    {
      person: { name, contact },  // typed by the person on the runner's
                                   // Applications page; never shown to the model
      sections: [
        {
          heading: string,        // one of the runner's fixed headings:
                                   // Summary, Experience, Projects, Open source,
                                   // Education, Certifications, Skills
          statements: [
            { text: string, claimIds: [string, ...] } // never empty — the
                                                        // validator refuses an
                                                        // uncited sentence
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
--}}
# {{person.name}}

{{#if person.contact}}
{{person.contact}}

{{/if}}
{{#each sections}}
## {{this.heading}}

{{#each this.statements}}
- {{this.text}}{{#each this.claimIds}} `[{{this}}]`{{/each}}
{{/each}}

{{/each}}
